n Prefers maximum long-term returns with maximum risk and principal fluctuations (15 points)
HOW WOULD THE CLIENT REACT TO A PORTFOLIO LOSING 20% OF ITS VALUE IN THE FIRST YEAR?
n Would be extremely concerned and liquidate the investment (3 points)
n Would be concerned and consider liquidating the investment (6 points)
n Would be concerned but not consider liquidating the investment (9 points)
n Would not be overly concerned given the long-term investment philosophy (12 points)
WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING EVENTS DOES THE CLIENT FEAR THE MOST?
n A loss of 10% of principal over a period of six months or less (3 points)
n A loss of 10% principal over a one-year period (6 points)
n Investment performance that consistently underperforms broad market benchmarks (9 points)
n A missed investment opportunity that may have yielded moderately higher returns over the long term
despite higher risk (12 points)
n A missed investment opportunity that may have yielded higher returns over the long term despite
substantially higher risk (15 points)
WHAT IS THE CLIENT'S OVERALL KNOWLEDGE OF INVESTMENTS?
n None (3 points)
n Low — Very little investment experience (6 points)
n Moderate — Some investment experience (9 points)
n High — Extensive investment experience (12 points)
ADDITIONAL INVESTMENT CONSTRAINTS
Carina has indicated a preference for ESG-aligned investments where possible. She also holds a concentrated
position in her employer's stock (~$85,000) which should be considered when evaluating large-cap domestic
equity exposure.
